Repair the following complete `solution.py`. Return a corrected complete source file.

`remap_points(points, source_size, target_size)` maps pixel coordinates between two rectangular grids. Sizes must be two-item sequences of non-boolean integers `(width, height)`, with each dimension at least 2. Points must be an iterable of two-item finite real coordinate sequences inside the inclusive source bounds `0..source_width-1` and `0..source_height-1`; booleans are invalid. Return new `(float, float)` tuples in input order, mapping both endpoints exactly via `x * (target_width - 1) / (source_width - 1)` and the equivalent formula for y. Empty points are valid. Do not mutate inputs. Wrong types raise `TypeError`; wrong lengths, sizes, or bounds raise `ValueError`.

